; A whole double below 10^16 is written out in an interpolation: 10, not
; 1e+01. eio.c's scaly_eio_format_double takes the shortest %g that reads
; back, and %g switches to the exponent form as soon as the exponent reaches
; the precision -- the shortest precision of 10.0 is one digit (2026-11-09,
; found writing the book's chapter on lanes: `a.sum()` printed "1e+01" beside
; "12"). A larger or a tiny value keeps the exponent.
let ten 10.0
let text "`ten` `1500.0` `500500.0` `1000000000000000.0` `10000000000000000.0` `1e21` `0.00001` `0.1` `-1000.0` `2.5` `0.0`"
if text.equals("10 1500 500500 1000000000000000 1e+16 1e+21 1e-05 0.1 -1000 2.5 0")
    print "PASS"
else
    print "FAIL `text`"
